WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:03.270
Film Courage: And you said one theater was
playing the film for over a year [without

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.270
your knowledge]?

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.270
Paul Sidhu: Yeah.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.270
I heard about it.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.639
I was kind of shocked.

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:14.799
Somebody…one of the guys who was actually
on the crew in India he called me up (I don’t

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:16.160
remember if he called me or emailed me).

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.619
He was like “Hey, Paul.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.259
I just saw your poster here.

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:23.650
It’s still up and they’re playing the
film.”

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.580
And I was like “Nahh, you’re full of it.”

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.740
And I was like “Come on man.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.919
Who is going to play that film for more than
a year?”

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:31.090
And he sent me a little picture and it was
up in the theater.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.329
And I was like “Damn!

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:33.480
They’re playing my film.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.559
It’s been up in the theater for like over
a year.”

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:40.620
So I decided to take a trip to go see like
what’s the story here?

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.371
Why do people like it?

00:00:42.371 --> 00:00:48.620
It was a pleasant surprise.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.890
The other thing that was also a pleasant surprise
was that first film was actually made it to

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.600
a lot of sources that I didn’t know about.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.910
This is the funniest story.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.399
So I told the theatrical rights.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:05.270
I got money for the theatrical rights.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.580
And that’s how we made our money.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.760
But we didn’t sell our television rights.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.480
So we’re shooting [Paul’s other film]
THE BLACK RUSSIAN up in the mountains and

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.170
there are only 2 channels.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:23.640
And on one of the public channels they’re
playing AAKHARI DECISION and this is crazy.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.470
So my crew (the make-up guy) he got sick.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.330
So he was the only guy who was laid up in
the hotel.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.740
And he was watching this and he sees my film.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:43.460
And in India they just assume that…since
this is a film you’re starring in they just

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.110
assume “He’s a well-known actor.”

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:51.210
And so he goes “Oh, there’s another one
of Paul’s films, it’s on TV.”

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:56.910
So he recorded it on his cell phone and he
said “Hey, your film is playing.”

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:57.910
And I’m like “My film is playing?

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:58.910
What are you talking about?

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.910
No ones playing it.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:00.910
This is my first film.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:01.910
How can my film be playing.”

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:02.910
And he’s like “No your film is playing.”

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:03.910
So I go “Well show me.”

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:07.190
So he recorded it and my first film was actually
playing.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:11.239
So we contacted the station.

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:13.379
We said “Hey who gave you the film?”

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:17.549
And they just didn’t answer the question.

00:02:17.549 --> 00:02:18.549
So that was cool!

00:02:18.549 --> 00:02:18.590
[Laughs]

